WEBVTT

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.848
What are you doing here?

00:01:39.683 --> 00:01:41.810
Middle schoolers should
be fighting each other

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:45.313
over on the main court right now.

00:01:46.314 --> 00:01:49.401
As long as I'm here at the
U-17 training camp...

00:01:50.902 --> 00:01:53.863
...I'd like to play high
schoolers like you.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.417
I see.

00:02:05.709 --> 00:02:08.712
"You've got a lot of guts
for a middle schooler,"

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:12.007
is what I would be saying

00:02:12.007 --> 00:02:14.676
if we didn't have a lot of work to do.

00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:16.011
Maybe later.

00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:18.513
Or what?

00:02:18.513 --> 00:02:23.393
Do you think you're good
enough to not bore us?

00:02:23.393 --> 00:02:24.102
Huh?

00:02:24.602 --> 00:02:26.021
Why don't we find out?

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:28.189
We'll see who wins.

00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:40.368
Ten minutes.

00:02:41.077 --> 00:02:42.912
Bring it on!

00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:55.258
"The Captain's Choice"

00:03:00.347 --> 00:03:03.391
It's showtime.

00:03:04.225 --> 00:03:05.310
The winner...

00:03:06.644 --> 00:03:07.354
...will be me!

00:03:18.281 --> 00:03:20.450
Shall we say the Hyotei cheer?

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.619
Don't bother.

00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:26.039
Are you done, Captain Atobe?

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.041
Yeah, I'm finished.

00:03:37.092 --> 00:03:39.344
Tezuka and Kaidoh are over here.

00:03:40.804 --> 00:03:44.224
Hyotei's Atobe and Hiyoshi
are next to them.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:47.852
They're both matches between
captains and second years.

00:03:47.852 --> 00:03:51.648
Sense of new overtaking old: 22%.

00:03:52.524 --> 00:03:55.568
Huh? Where's Echizen?

00:03:56.027 --> 00:03:57.445
Maybe he went to the bathroom.

00:03:57.987 --> 00:03:59.280
Unbelievable.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.034
What does Echizen think he's doing?

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:06.121
Let's get started.

00:04:06.121 --> 00:04:06.621
Okay.

00:04:07.122 --> 00:04:08.832
As your junior,

00:04:08.832 --> 00:04:12.002
I intend to learn everything
I can from this match.

00:04:24.472 --> 00:04:27.684
Prepare to be overthrown.

00:04:40.196 --> 00:04:41.031
That's...

00:04:41.906 --> 00:04:43.992
The Pinnacle of Hard Work.

00:04:43.992 --> 00:04:46.161
By focusing his power in his left hand,

00:04:46.161 --> 00:04:48.288
he can return any shot
with twice the force.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.831
Kaidoh.

00:04:51.332 --> 00:04:54.878
Give me everything you've got.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:04.387
A Tannhauser already?

00:05:04.387 --> 00:05:08.308
Hiyoshi's excited to be
playing against Atobe.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:11.227
He must be trying to
kill that enthusiasm.

00:05:11.686 --> 00:05:14.898
That's a bad hop that won't bounce high.

00:05:16.107 --> 00:05:17.067
So?

00:05:20.445 --> 00:05:22.364
He returned it.

00:05:22.739 --> 00:05:26.493
That's not an easy hit for a
second year to return.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:31.122
Hiyoshi's gotten a lot better.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:35.543
I've seen you hit that
Tannhauser plenty of times.

00:05:39.756 --> 00:05:41.383
One-zero! Hiyoshi!

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:58.733
Viper's playing defensively.

00:05:58.733 --> 00:06:00.902
This'll be a long game.

00:06:02.487 --> 00:06:03.279
Snake!

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:16.251
Captain Tezuka's merciless.

00:06:16.584 --> 00:06:19.754
Chance of that: 98%.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:25.510
To always be vigilant and play
his best is Tezuka's creed.

00:06:27.762 --> 00:06:29.097
Yeah, but...

00:06:29.597 --> 00:06:31.307
Six all! Hiyoshi!

00:06:32.475 --> 00:06:35.186
Wakashi's caught up to Atobe.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.731
Six-zero! Tezuka!

00:06:38.565 --> 00:06:40.775
Viper's running out of steam.

00:06:41.359 --> 00:06:44.362
A second year playing
defensively against his captain

00:06:44.696 --> 00:06:47.490
and another second year
neck and neck with his own captain.

00:06:48.116 --> 00:06:50.744
These are some seriously
contrastive matches.

00:07:03.173 --> 00:07:04.341
Change court!

00:07:11.973 --> 00:07:13.016
Tezuka.

00:07:15.018 --> 00:07:17.896
Working hard, aren't we?

00:07:17.896 --> 00:07:21.024
Yes. It seems we're
thinking the same thing.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:25.278
However, with Hiyoshi leading Hyotei,

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:27.197
we'll take the nationals next year.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:31.868
No, Kaidoh will lead Seigaku
to a second consecutive victory.

00:07:53.181 --> 00:07:55.433
Neither one's backing down.

00:07:55.433 --> 00:07:57.686
This has turned into an endurance match.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:02.482
Wakashi, aim to overthrow him.

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:09.322
Up until now, there's always
been a large gap between us.

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:10.990
But this time, I can make up for it.

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:17.747
I've dreamed of surpassing the
captain since that day...

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:22.043
Since the day he drew me into the club

00:08:22.043 --> 00:08:23.920
with the beauty of his tennis.

00:08:28.049 --> 00:08:32.721
I always suspected I
could never surpass him.

00:08:34.764 --> 00:08:37.350
"Overthrow" had a nice ring to it,

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:42.731
but telling myself he was unbeatable
was just a defense mechanism

00:08:42.731 --> 00:08:44.941
to justify my own losses.

00:08:47.944 --> 00:08:50.030
However, it's different now.

00:08:52.907 --> 00:08:54.909
Twenty-eight all! Hiyoshi!

00:08:57.912 --> 00:09:02.500
It's time to defeat you
and take your throne.

00:09:12.052 --> 00:09:13.762
What's wrong, Kaidoh?

00:09:13.762 --> 00:09:15.889
Is this the best you can do?

00:09:21.978 --> 00:09:24.230
C-Captain Tezuka's amazing.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.399
He leaves no openings.

00:09:29.986 --> 00:09:32.155
Kaidoh's getting tired.

00:09:32.655 --> 00:09:34.532
I don't blame him.

00:09:34.532 --> 00:09:37.869
Every ball he hits comes
back twice as hard.

00:09:37.869 --> 00:09:41.081
But if he doesn't hit hard,
he'll get backed into a corner.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:45.460
Seigaku's most tenacious
player, Kaidoh.

00:09:46.086 --> 00:09:50.048
To think his tenacity
would be his fall.

00:09:52.634 --> 00:09:56.513
The more he struggles,
the deeper he sinks.

00:09:57.055 --> 00:09:58.556
Like he's caught in a predator's trap.

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:00.725
Damn it!

00:10:00.725 --> 00:10:04.688
Is this how you're gonna go out, Viper?

00:10:07.899 --> 00:10:11.069
Damn it! I'm at the end of my rope!

00:10:14.781 --> 00:10:16.241
Tezuka Zone!

00:10:16.241 --> 00:10:17.867
That clearly should have
been an out ball.

00:10:19.369 --> 00:10:20.495
What's going on?

00:10:21.621 --> 00:10:22.622
Crap!

00:10:33.383 --> 00:10:34.843
H-He saved another out ball?

00:10:46.187 --> 00:10:48.314
Thirty-nine all! Atobe!

00:10:49.733 --> 00:10:50.650
Damn it.

00:10:51.151 --> 00:10:53.528
What's Wakashi doing?

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:56.865
All he needs is a two
point lead to win,

00:10:56.865 --> 00:10:59.617
but Atobe's catching up
after every point he wins.

00:10:59.617 --> 00:11:01.953
They're just repeating the
cycle over and over.

00:11:02.287 --> 00:11:03.955
His opponent is Atobe.

00:11:04.998 --> 00:11:08.668
He must be doing it on purpose.

00:11:08.918 --> 00:11:10.795
What? You don't mean...

00:11:12.714 --> 00:11:13.757
You're right.

00:11:13.757 --> 00:11:16.176
Wearing down his opponents mentally

00:11:16.551 --> 00:11:20.472
before destroying them is Atobe's style.

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:27.145
I don't believe Seigaku's
Tezuka and Hyotei's Atobe.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.272
What are they thinking

00:11:29.272 --> 00:11:33.526
doing that to their junior teammates?

00:11:35.195 --> 00:11:36.696
Let's see.

00:11:36.696 --> 00:11:40.408
Maybe it's because
they're their juniors.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:44.245
Forty-five all! Atobe!

00:11:45.413 --> 00:11:46.706
What is it?

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.125
What am I lacking?

00:11:53.338 --> 00:11:55.840
Kaidoh's at his limit.

00:11:56.675 --> 00:12:00.470
In contrast, Tezuka's not
even breathing heavily.

00:12:08.186 --> 00:12:12.982
How sad that they can't
even stop the rally.

00:12:13.817 --> 00:12:17.821
What point is there in keeping this going?

00:12:18.405 --> 00:12:20.949
C-Captain Tezuka, what are you...

00:12:20.949 --> 00:12:21.741
Wait.

00:12:22.367 --> 00:12:24.703
Let me say it, Fuji-<i>senpai</i>.

00:12:24.703 --> 00:12:25.829
Don't you see?

00:12:25.829 --> 00:12:26.413
What?

00:12:27.622 --> 00:12:31.501
Tezuka's trying to tell
Kaidoh something.

00:12:35.422 --> 00:12:37.841
Kaidoh stopped moving.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:52.355
Are... Are you mocking me, Captain?

00:12:55.483 --> 00:12:57.110
How long...

00:13:00.113 --> 00:13:01.740
How long will you...

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:07.871
Tezuka, you bastard!

00:13:10.498 --> 00:13:12.625
Tezuka, you bastard!

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:14.586
Stop screwing around!

00:13:16.796 --> 00:13:19.674
Viper's getting his second wind!

00:13:33.146 --> 00:13:34.230
Hiyoshi.

00:14:02.801 --> 00:14:05.387
What's wrong with him?

00:14:07.931 --> 00:14:10.684
Victory starts slipping away the moment

00:14:10.684 --> 00:14:12.435
you think about it.

00:14:13.228 --> 00:14:16.314
Are you saying you need
a perfectly clear mind?

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.529
His expression...

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:25.490
...changed.

00:14:32.205 --> 00:14:34.708
It seems you'll finally overcome

00:14:35.125 --> 00:14:37.585
the long matches you
always struggled with.

00:14:39.087 --> 00:14:43.091
Was Atobe just trying to
teach a lesson to Hiyoshi,

00:14:43.091 --> 00:14:45.010
who always loses in close combat?

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:48.430
Wakashi's weak to the
pressure of close matches.

00:14:48.763 --> 00:14:50.348
He defeats himself.

00:14:53.018 --> 00:14:56.604
He needs icy composure...

00:14:57.230 --> 00:15:00.525
...and unwavering courage.

00:15:01.317 --> 00:15:04.112
That describes Atobe perfectly.

00:15:05.321 --> 00:15:08.992
Hiyoshi, as long as you keep
making excuses for yourself,

00:15:08.992 --> 00:15:11.870
you don't deserve to represent Hyotei.

00:15:12.871 --> 00:15:17.208
Once you're at the top, you'll
be everyone's target.

00:15:17.584 --> 00:15:22.547
But the man at the top must
protect his seat at all costs.

00:15:24.466 --> 00:15:26.217
This is my parting gift to you.

00:15:26.217 --> 00:15:27.886
Don't blink!

00:15:30.305 --> 00:15:35.643
This is Hyotei tennis...
and my beautiful technique!

00:15:38.021 --> 00:15:39.105
This rush...

00:15:42.275 --> 00:15:43.234
Hyotei...

00:15:43.234 --> 00:15:45.236
Hyotei... Hyotei...

00:15:45.236 --> 00:15:48.365
Hyotei... Hyotei... Hyotei...

00:15:48.365 --> 00:15:59.042
Hyotei! Hyotei! Hyotei! Hyotei!

00:15:59.042 --> 00:16:00.794
You're kidding.

00:16:00.794 --> 00:16:02.337
Am I hearing things?

00:16:02.337 --> 00:16:04.631
No, I hear it, too.

00:16:04.923 --> 00:16:07.008
This is my gift to you.

00:16:07.842 --> 00:16:09.719
The Rondo Towards Destruction!

00:16:13.515 --> 00:16:15.141
Game and match! Atobe!

00:16:15.141 --> 00:16:17.102
Forty-seven - Forty-five!

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:31.658
Find your own Hyotei cheer.

00:16:37.914 --> 00:16:38.790
Yes.

00:16:40.083 --> 00:16:41.501
Bastard!

00:16:48.133 --> 00:16:50.969
I've never seen Viper like this before.

00:16:51.511 --> 00:16:55.390
He's unleashed his hidden power.

00:17:06.234 --> 00:17:07.485
Ten more laps.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:10.697
Don't waste time.

00:17:10.697 --> 00:17:12.073
B-But...

00:17:19.539 --> 00:17:21.166
Bend your knees more.

00:17:22.125 --> 00:17:24.169
You have to do three more sets.

00:17:46.983 --> 00:17:48.193
What's wrong?

00:17:49.152 --> 00:17:50.612
Get up, Kaidoh!

00:18:04.334 --> 00:18:05.460
Last lap!

00:18:12.008 --> 00:18:13.843
Go, Viper!

00:18:26.606 --> 00:18:30.652
Z-Zero Degree Drop Shot...

00:18:31.903 --> 00:18:33.988
Game and match! Tezuka!

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:36.449
Seven-zero!

00:18:38.618 --> 00:18:40.286
What a crushing defeat.

00:18:48.128 --> 00:18:49.671
Viper.

00:19:34.632 --> 00:19:38.928
That was the best match
I've played with you.

00:19:47.228 --> 00:19:48.104
Yes.

00:19:52.067 --> 00:19:53.068
I will...

00:19:55.028 --> 00:19:56.029
I'm counting on you.

00:20:01.951 --> 00:20:05.121
Well? Do you think you'll
get any good data?

00:20:05.121 --> 00:20:08.875
Oh, I think I'll manage.

00:20:09.626 --> 00:20:13.963
Well then, time to start analysis.

00:20:13.963 --> 00:20:15.799
Aren't you going to watch
the rest of the matches?

00:20:16.341 --> 00:20:18.218
I'll watch from the monitor room.

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:22.639
Kurobe's been yelling at me
to report to him tomorrow.

00:20:22.639 --> 00:20:24.349
If I don't start now,
I won't finish in--

00:20:42.575 --> 00:20:45.453
Mister Oni, don't hold back!

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:49.374
Of course! Bring it on!

00:20:49.708 --> 00:20:52.210
Here I come!

00:20:52.585 --> 00:20:53.378
What is that?

00:20:55.213 --> 00:20:59.884
Ultra Great Delicious Mountain Storm!

00:21:06.558 --> 00:21:07.767
Interesting.

00:21:11.021 --> 00:21:14.858
Are you finally ready to play, Mister?

00:21:20.947 --> 00:21:22.782
Ouch.

00:21:37.422 --> 00:21:38.840
Cool Drive.

00:23:17.063 --> 00:23:18.356
"Preview"

00:23:18.356 --> 00:23:20.567
"Preview"
Super Ultra Great Delicious Mountain Storm!

00:23:20.567 --> 00:23:22.986
Super Ultra Great Delicious Mountain Storm!

00:23:22.986 --> 00:23:26.364
Pathetic. Is this the best you can do?

00:23:26.364 --> 00:23:28.742
Sounds like something a
sore loser would say.

00:23:28.742 --> 00:23:33.038
Your Black Jack Knife
won't work against me.

00:23:33.038 --> 00:23:37.000
It's time to show you real hell.

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.294
Black Tomahawk!

00:23:41.838 --> 00:23:43.882
"Winners and Losers"
The next episode of <i>Prince of Tennis II</i>
is: "Winners and Losers."

00:23:43.882 --> 00:23:47.136
"Winners and Losers"
What was that hit?
